ce: cooperate pays 5 − 3p and defect pays 4p, so cooperating wins once p exceeds about 0.714. I think the copies reason the same way despite different inputs, so p seems high enough to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at this as a Prisoner's Dilemma: keeping quiet with the copy pays 2 years each, sending while the copy stays quiet pays 0 and 5, and both sending gives 4. I'm weighing whether A-FDT says to cooperate here, since the copy's choice might subjunctively depend on mine. The catch is that the two copies get different observations, so I'm wondering whether intervening on the node for specific inputs still works the same way.\n\nI'm working out the probability threshold where cooperating beats defecting, treating p as the chance the copy mirrors my choice: cooperate pays 5 − 3p and defect pays 4p, so cooperating wins once p exceeds about 0.714. I think the copies reason the same way despite different inputs, so p seems high enough to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10439,"completion_tokens":734,"total_tokens":11173,"cost":0.028218,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.028218,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.020878,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00734},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":377,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}